The issue is caused by `cbook._safe_first_finite` being called on an array that contains only `NaN` values. When `x0` (the first coordinate of the bar positions) consists only of `NaN`s, `_safe_first_finite` attempts to find the first finite value using a generator expression, which raises `StopIteration` when no such value exists.

The `_convert_dx` method in `Axes._convert_dx` is designed to handle width conversion. It uses `_safe_first_finite` to get a representative finite value from `x0` and `xconv` to perform calculations that might involve units (like `datetime` and `timedelta`). If the input arrays are all `NaN`, this should be caught gracefully.

In `_convert_dx`, the code already has `try...except` blocks around these calls, but they only catch `TypeError`, `IndexError`, and `KeyError`. We need to expand this to catch `StopIteration` as well.

